          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चावणो (chāvṇo) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from cāh, \"see, look for, desire\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants. CDIAL lists Old Marwari cāhaï under it (CDIAL 4775). CDIAL calls the further source of this reconstructed verb uncertain."
